<Base title="Privacy and optional analytics" description="How Acquisition Companion handles optional analytics, local progress, search, and AI Deal Lab." type="About"><Crumbs items={[{title:'Privacy'}]}/><article class="narrow"><header class="page-header"><p class="eyebrow">Your choice</p><h1>Privacy and analytics.</h1></header><div class="prose"><p>Acquisition Companion is free to read without an account. Lesson progress and your analytics choice are saved in this browser. Site search runs locally in your browser.</p><h2 id="ai-deal-lab">Optional AI Deal Lab</h2><p>AI Deal Lab is an optional educational tool. Questions, a short capped conversation context, and the selected synthetic case stage are sent to OpenAI to generate a response. The server sends API requests with <code>store: false</code> and Acquisition Companion does not intentionally maintain a server-side chat history. This setting is not a zero-retention guarantee; OpenAI’s applicable policies may still govern its processing.</p><p>Do not submit confidential, proprietary, personal, or non-public deal information. Version 1 has no private deal-document, CIM, or data-room uploads. Conversation context stays in the active page session and is not saved as a chat history by this site.</p><p>AI Deal Lab analytics events remain subject to the same consent choice as the rest of the site. They may include a selected mode, synthetic case identifier, difficulty, or completion status. Google Analytics does not receive question text, answer text, prompts, response contents, financial figures entered in chat, company names, or conversation transcripts.</p><h2>Optional Google Analytics</h2><p>If you choose “Allow analytics,” the site loads Google Analytics to understand aggregate site usage. It can record page views, course starts, completed lessons, searches, clicks to original YouTube sources, and non-sensitive AI Deal Lab activity. Search events include the term only when it exactly matches a short list of educational topics; other searches are recorded without the text. We do not send transcript text to Google.</p><p>You can choose “No thanks” and use the entire site. Google Analytics does not load before consent or after a decline. No advertising, remarketing, or advertising personalization is enabled.</p><p>Use <strong>Analytics preferences</strong> in the footer to change your choice. Changing from allow to decline reloads the page to stop the active analytics script. Following an external source link takes you to that site’s own privacy practices.</p></div></article></Base>
